resistance to florfenicol and chloramphenicol.</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source> <year>1999</year>;<volume>37</volume>:<fpage>1348</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10203484</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R8"><label>8. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Kim</surname> <given-names>EH</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Aoki</surname> <given-names>T</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Drug resistance and broad geographical distribution of identical R plasmids of <italic>Pasteurella piscicida</italic> isolated from cultured yellowtail in Japan.</article-title><source>Microbiol Immunol</source> <year>1993</year>;<volume>37</volume>:<fpage>103</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8502175</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R9"><label>9. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Cloeckaert</surname> <given-names>A</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Baucheron</surname> <given-names>S</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Chaslus-Dancla</surname> <given-names>E</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Nonenzymatic chloramphenicol resistance mediated by IncC plasmid R55 is encoded by a <italic>floR</italic> gene variant.</article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents Chemother</source> <year>2001</year>;<volume>45</volume>:<fpage>2381</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>2</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/AAC.45.8.2381-2382.2001</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11451703</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Chabbert</surname> <given-names>YA</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Scavizzi</surname> <given-names>MR</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Witchitz</surname> <given-names>JL</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Gerbaud</surname> <given-names>GR</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>